LMMS 1.2.2 reference runtime: licence and corresponding source

lmms-1.2.2-linux-x86_64.AppImage in this directory is the unmodified upstream
release asset of LMMS 1.2.2 (GitHub release v1.2.2; 96362536 bytes,
sha256 6cdc45a0699b8cd85295c49bcac03fcce6f3d8ffd7da23d646d0cb4258869b76).
solve.sh checks that digest and unpacks the image with the AppImage's own
extractor (--appimage-extract) into runtime/. The installer then omits the
optional VeSTige, Carla base, Carla Rack, Carla Patchbay and external LADSPA host modules.
Remaining executable and library bytes are unchanged. The launcher launch.py, start.sh, solve.sh and the preload
library lmms_cpus.so with its source lmms_cpus.c are this repository's own
files and are not part of LMMS. lmms_cpus.so is built from lmms_cpus.c with
gcc 11.4 (Ubuntu 22.04, glibc 2.35):
  gcc -O2 -fPIC -shared -Wl,--build-id=none -o lmms_cpus.so lmms_cpus.c -ldl
It only lowers the processor count that sysconf and get_nprocs report to the
LMMS process, so that LMMS starts no more mixer threads than its CPU quota
allows.

