The local isolation.py adapter requires enabled Landlock ABI 1 or newer and
uses the filesystem rights supported by that ABI. File writes, creation and
removal are restricted to the configured instance/document directories and
the required /dev/null and /dev/shm paths. Execution is limited to the selected
product binary and the dynamic loader. ABI 1 denies cross-directory renames
and hard links. On ABI 2 or newer, these operations are permitted only where
the applicable Landlock path rules allow them. File truncation is restricted
only on ABI 3 or newer; the adapter provides no truncation restriction on
ABI 1 or 2. It does not modify upstream executable bytes.
